Architecture checkpoint after Sprint 4:

    Report is the domain model.
    JSON is the first serializer, not the core model.
    Renderers receive Report only.
    Flask, CLI, Designer, AI, and future adapters should target Report.
    YAML, XML plugins, REST, binary, and database storage belong at the serializer/storage boundary.

Sprint 4 review answers:

    Beginners can build reports with Report and page helpers before learning JSON.
    AI should generate the same Report API that humans use, or serializer input at the boundary.
    Designer, Flask, and CLI can manipulate Report directly.
    JSON can become optional once storage and serializers are cleanly separated.
    YAML can be added later as a serializer.
    XML can live as a plugin serializer.
    Database storage can serialize or decompose Report, but loading must return Report.

Sprint 5 Canvas checkpoint:

    Designer UI is a framework-agnostic static package.
    Flask, Django, FastAPI, and other adapters should host the same UI files.
    Adapters provide APIs for template load/save, preview, and PDF export.
    The Canvas edits Slim Report JSON in the browser and sends it to serializers at the boundary.
    No React, Vue, TypeScript, Fabric.js, or build step yet.
